## Facts worth knowing before you search
- **Only customer >10%:** FUJIFILM Electronic Materials Taiwan, 10,675m yen = 13.9% of FY03/2026 sales (12.9% in FY03/2025, below 10% before). Yuho P30/P100. About 26% of Electronic Materials sales [I: 10,675 / 41,515].
- **No HBM or AI revenue share is disclosed anywhere.** The only HBM mention is the architecture diagram on deck slide 35 (hybrid bonding). TSMC is named once: "Adopted for TSMC N2-generation nodes" (deck slide 30).
- **No Fuso Q&A transcript is in the folder.** The briefings of 12-Nov-2025 and 15-May-2026 were held for institutional investors (tanshin cover), but the deck divider "Q&A" has no content. Q3 FY03/2026 and Q1 FY03/2027 had no briefing. Use the Dialogue summary (06) for the themes investors press, and the Nissan Chemical / Mitsubishi Chemical Q&A files only for how analysts frame peers.
- **Benzene is quoted as ENEOS ACP price** (USD/t). FY03/2025 average 996, FY03/2026 average 745, Apr-May 2026 1,130 (deck slide 25).
- **Depreciation is declining-balance (定率法), machinery 4-8 years** (yuho P75), so each new plant is front-loaded in cost.
- **Subsidy:** 3,694m yen granted 15-Jun-2026 for the Kyoto new line already built (Oct-2024), booked as extraordinary income in FY03/2027 (yuho P104). It reimburses past capex; it does not fund the 40,000m project.

## Open conflicts and gaps
- **FY03/2027 net income guidance:** 16,600 (deck and tanshin of 11/15-May-2026, EPS 156.90) vs 19,200 (Q1 tanshin 7-Aug-2026, EPS 181.48, marked "no revision"). The 2,600m gap equals 3,694m x (1 - about 29.6%), in line with the subsidy gain, and the H1 forecast moves by the same 2,600m (7,850 to 10,450). Sales and OP are unchanged. Reading: **consistent with the Aug figure including the subsidy** [I]; the Workspace "guidance" is probably newer, not wrong. A TDnet notice of mid-June to Aug-2026 is not in the folder; fetch it to close this.
- The model sheet `Fuso Financials` row 93 labels the Q1 FY03/2027 extraordinary income 3,703.86 as "gain on sale of fixed assets". It is **subsidy income** (Q1 tanshin P5).
- Missing: Japanese Q1 FY03/2027 tanshin; any Q1 segment data; Q&A notes of the 15-May-2026 briefing; yuho FY03/2024 and earlier (needed for FY03/2024 trough explanation: only FY03/2025 comparatives exist here).
